Chapter: T3 Gate

 The gate program for the T3ISA plug. Arithmetic, recursion and control
 flow over bounded integers, with output through the emulator's syscalls.
 It stays small on purpose: the whole T3ISA address space is 65,536 words,
 and the emulator's step budget is finite.

 Every band is declared. A bare Integer is the full 64-bit range, which
 does not fit a 27-trit word, and the plug refuses it rather than emitting
 arithmetic that saturates. That refusal is F4 in the design and this
 program is what demonstrates the boundary is real: widen any band past
 3,812,798,742,493 and the compile stops.

Section: Body

  fib : Integer between 0 and 1000000 -> Integer between 0 and 1000000
  fib (n) = if n <= 1 then n else fib (n - 1) + fib (n - 2)

  gcd : Integer between 0 and 1000000, Integer between 0 and 1000000 -> Integer between 0 and 1000000
  gcd (a) (b) = if b == 0 then a else gcd b (__narrow (int-mod a b))

  collatz-len : Integer between 0 and 1000000, Integer between 0 and 1000000 -> Integer between 0 and 1000000
  collatz-len (n) (acc) =
   if n <= 1 then acc
   else if int-mod n 2 == 0 then collatz-len (n / 2) (acc + 1)
   else collatz-len (n * 3 + 1) (acc + 1)

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("fib 20 = " & show (fib 20))
    print-line-uni ("gcd 1071 462 = " & show (gcd 1071 462))
    print-line-uni ("collatz 27 = " & show (collatz-len 27 0))
  end
